    "faq": {
      "type": "plugpal-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q_1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is it safe to plug this much into one outlet?",
            "answer": "<p>For everyday electronics, yes. Plug-Pal has a surge circuit, a flame-retardant housing and a screw mount that keeps it from sagging out of the wall. What matters is total load: everything shares one 15A / 1,875W circuit. Phones, lamps, TVs and a coffee maker are fine.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What shouldn't I plug into it?",
            "answer": "<p>Plug space heaters, hair dryers, straighteners and window AC units straight into the wall, and don't run two heat appliances at once (kettle and toaster, air fryer and microwave). Plug-Pal adds sockets, not power: if something trips your breaker today, it'll trip it on Plug-Pal too. It isn't a GFCI.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will it fit my outlet?",
            "answer": "<p>It fits standard US and Canadian two-socket, 3-prong grounded outlets with a centre screw in the cover plate. Deep plates may need the longer 6-32 screw, which is in the box.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "My outlets are 2-prong. Will it work?",
            "answer": "<p>No. Plug-Pal has a 3-prong grounded plug, so it needs a 3-prong outlet. Older homes often have 2-prong outlets in some rooms, so check before you order.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does it block the light switch or the other socket?",
            "answer": "<p>It covers both sockets of the outlet and turns them into nine ports. On a combined switch-and-outlet plate it sits beside the switch. Add the exact dimensions from your sample here.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will the USB-C port charge my laptop?",
            "answer": "<p>No. The USB ports are for phones, earbuds, watches and controllers. Laptops and large tablets need their own charger, which you can plug into one of the five AC outlets.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_7": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is the night light bright enough? Does it stay on all night?",
            "answer": "<p>It's a soft glow made for hallways, bathrooms and nurseries, not a room light. The sensor turns it on at dusk and off when the room gets light. Tap the light icon to set the brightness.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_8": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does the surge protection last?",
            "answer": "<p>Surge protection is rated in joules, and each big surge uses some of it up. The protected-indicator light shows it's still working. If the light goes out, the outlets still work but surge protection doesn't, so replace the unit.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_9": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need an electrician?",
            "answer": "<p>No. There's no wiring. You need a flat-head or Phillips screwdriver and about 30 seconds.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_10": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "I rent. Can I use it?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. It doesn't change your wiring and it leaves no marks. When you move, unscrew it, put your old cover-plate screw back and take Plug-Pal with you.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_11": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "My outlet is loose. Will Plug-Pal hold it?",
            "answer": "<p>No, and you shouldn't try. If an outlet is loose, cracked, sunken into the wall or won't hold a screw, have it repaired first. Plug-Pal needs a solid outlet.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_12": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does it work in my country?",
            "answer": "<p>Plug-Pal is made for US and Canadian outlets (Type B, 120V). It won't fit outlets in the UK, Europe or Australia.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
